    {
      "kind": "chapter",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Start from a template instead of a blank page"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narration",
      "text": "A template is a starting text in a design that suits it: a report with a cover page and contents, a paper with a title block and numbered sections, a runbook with numbered steps and framed commands. Demo, picked for your first document, is a short tour of markdown and of markoto itself; Blank is an empty page in your default design. Grey comments in each skeleton say what goes where; the preview and the PDF never show them.",
      "file": "04.webp",
      "cursor": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 425
      },
      "path": "/"
    },
    {
      "kind": "chapter",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "A picture of every template"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narration",
      "text": "Each card shows the template's first page in its design, its name and one line about what is in it. The tabs sort them by who they are for: engineering, academic, business, writing.",
